WEBVTT

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:05.980
Senriyama Station

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:13.050
Toki, wait up!

00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:17.590
Ryuka?

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:24.210
This was the first time you've 
come to the club in a while.

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:28.580
Did the doctor finally 
say it's okay to come?

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:31.380
Yeah. Well...

00:00:32.110 --> 00:00:34.170
he told me not to overdo it.

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:35.630
Overdo?

00:00:37.490 --> 00:00:39.390
Like you and Sera.

00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:41.800
Ah!

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:44.060
Does that mean you watched 
the national's match?

00:00:44.990 --> 00:00:47.320
I do have lots of time at the hospital.

00:00:47.320 --> 00:00:49.030
How embarrassing!

00:00:49.030 --> 00:00:51.950
I made the regular team as a 2nd year,

00:00:51.950 --> 00:00:54.030
but I wasn't able to do 
anything in the finals.

00:00:54.340 --> 00:00:55.330
Well,

00:00:56.120 --> 00:00:58.430
the match was practically decided

00:00:58.430 --> 00:01:00.740
before you could do anything.

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:08.460
If you were watching, 
I'm sure you saw...

00:01:09.170 --> 00:01:11.230
When Shiraitodai won...

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:13.450
Miyanaga-san, huh?

00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:16.090
Kind of unbelievable that 
she's just a 2nd year.

00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:17.880
Nationals are just that amazing.

00:01:18.430 --> 00:01:22.460
We 2nd years will be 
the major force next year.

00:01:22.460 --> 00:01:23.890
I guess so.

00:01:23.890 --> 00:01:25.710
Good luck as the new captain.

00:01:25.710 --> 00:01:27.670
What are you muttering about?

00:01:27.670 --> 00:01:29.480
We're the same year.

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:33.110
But I'm sickly.

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:36.240
Are we back to that again?

00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:40.400
Well, it's a fact that 
I'm just a ghost member.

00:01:43.050 --> 00:01:44.330
I have to go.

00:01:45.110 --> 00:01:50.440
My doctor gets really mad if 
I'm late for my appointment.

00:01:51.050 --> 00:01:52.020
Bye.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:55.630
Hey, Toki?

00:01:58.010 --> 00:02:02.760
Want to go to the nationals with me?

00:02:23.030 --> 00:02:24.240
Good morning.

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:28.600
Oh yeah.

00:02:28.600 --> 00:02:29.750
I...

00:02:30.180 --> 00:02:31.570
Are you awake?

00:02:31.570 --> 00:02:33.630
The match is in 15 minutes.

00:02:33.950 --> 00:02:38.380
You think we'll be okay without going over 
our opponents' data one last time?

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:40.100
Yeah.

00:02:45.690 --> 00:02:47.140
Did you sleep well?

00:02:47.590 --> 00:02:48.590
A dream.

00:02:48.590 --> 00:02:49.270
Huh?

00:02:50.090 --> 00:02:52.120
I had a dream.

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:26.910
<b>Round 5: 
Veteran</b>

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:35.000
Did I miss anything?!

00:04:35.470 --> 00:04:36.930
They're still doing the introduction.

00:04:36.930 --> 00:04:38.510
I made it!

00:04:38.510 --> 00:04:41.840
I guess the pro player, Mihirogi, 
is the analyst again.

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:41.840
<b>Analyst
Mihirogi Eiko</b>

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:45.140
It's the fifth day of the Inter-high tournament.

00:04:45.140 --> 00:04:47.100
Today we start the second round matches.

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:49.600
Of our eight schools playing today,

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:52.600
four will advance to the semi-finals.

00:04:53.120 --> 00:04:57.100
The second of the second round matches
 are moving to the tournament hall.

00:04:57.500 --> 00:04:58.920
<i>Having lost in the first round</i>

00:04:58.920 --> 00:05:01.310
<i>in their previous four appearances,</i>

00:05:01.310 --> 00:05:06.020
<i>Saitama Prefecture's 
Koshigaya Girls' Academy</i>

00:05:06.020 --> 00:05:07.700
<i>finally finds itself 
competing in Round Two.</i>

00:05:07.410 --> 00:05:09.620
Saitama Prefecture Representative
Koshigaya Girls'
Arai Sophia (3rd year)

00:05:07.700 --> 00:05:09.620
<i>Their first player is Arai Sophia.</i>

00:05:10.210 --> 00:05:12.110
<i>Having survived one of the most</i>

00:05:12.110 --> 00:05:13.550
<i>furious preliminaries 
in Hyougo Prefecture,</i>

00:05:13.550 --> 00:05:16.870
<i>Kentani High has prevailed in 
the first round against Ibaraki</i>

00:05:16.870 --> 00:05:20.410
<i>and Shizuoka, and sends Tsubakino Miyuki.</i>

00:05:18.630 --> 00:05:21.130
Hyougo Prefecture Representative 
Kentani High School
Tsubakino Miyuki (3rd year)

00:05:21.390 --> 00:05:23.020
Should be coming soon now.

00:05:23.020 --> 00:05:23.960
Maybe next?

00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:26.510
<i>Up next is Nara Prefecture's 
representative.</i>

00:05:26.510 --> 00:05:27.720
Here they are!

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:29.830
<i>Achiga Girls' Academy.</i>

00:05:29.830 --> 00:05:32.070
<i>This is their second appearance in ten years.</i>

00:05:32.070 --> 00:05:34.160
<i>Their first player will be Matsumi Kuro.</i>

00:05:32.220 --> 00:05:39.480
Nara Prefecture Representative
Achiga Girls' Academy
 Matsumi Kuro (2nd year)

00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:36.100
<i>They are being coached by the</i>

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:38.680
<i>star of their previous team, Akado Harue,</i>

00:05:38.680 --> 00:05:40.770
<i>who made it to the quarter 
finals ten years ago.</i>

00:05:39.480 --> 00:05:40.770
Kuro-chan!

00:05:40.770 --> 00:05:41.860
Matsumi-senpai!

00:05:41.860 --> 00:05:42.980
Good luck!

00:05:44.450 --> 00:05:46.080
The seed school that will

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:47.910
participate beginning this round is

00:05:47.910 --> 00:05:50.430
Senriyama Girl's Academy, 
who have competed a total

00:05:50.430 --> 00:05:52.340
of thirty-five times in this tournament!

00:05:52.340 --> 00:05:54.340
They have dominated the competitive

00:05:54.340 --> 00:05:58.540
North Osaka region for eleven straight years,

00:05:58.540 --> 00:06:00.280
and send Onjouji Toki in first.

00:06:03.470 --> 00:06:06.840
Thanks for helping me back then.

00:06:09.770 --> 00:06:13.780
Hey, that's the girl who was 
eating the eel bun at Hanamatsu!

00:06:13.780 --> 00:06:16.310
We were eating that, too.

00:06:16.850 --> 00:06:18.430
Onjouji Toki...

00:06:19.200 --> 00:06:21.300
There's practically no data

00:06:21.300 --> 00:06:23.740
on her official matches 
older than last year.

00:06:25.180 --> 00:06:28.610
From this round, the top two 
schools will be advancing.

00:06:28.610 --> 00:06:30.580
The top two schools will advance, you say?

00:06:30.580 --> 00:06:33.530
Shouldn't it be a little 
more cutthroat?

00:06:33.530 --> 00:06:35.410
You think so?

00:06:35.410 --> 00:06:38.790
We're already eliminating half,
 like any other tournament.

00:06:39.370 --> 00:06:42.540
Additionally, there is a 
high degree of randomness.

00:06:42.880 --> 00:06:46.550
The road to the top is 
narrow, rough, and long.

00:06:47.010 --> 00:06:50.540
These girls will only have a 
brief window of opportunity.

00:06:51.540 --> 00:06:55.310
<i>I can't see how that isn't harsh enough.</i>

00:06:56.950 --> 00:07:00.810
71st National High School Mahjong 
Championship Tournament

00:06:57.320 --> 00:07:00.530
<i>Hmm, you think so?</i>

00:07:01.560 --> 00:07:03.290
<i>The seats have been decided.</i>

00:07:03.290 --> 00:07:04.940
<i>The first players' match will begin shortly.</i>

00:07:07.120 --> 00:07:09.360
Let the match begin!

00:07:13.730 --> 00:07:14.740
<i>All right!</i>

00:07:14.740 --> 00:07:15.990
<i>I'm going to give it my best.</i>

00:07:31.780 --> 00:07:34.140
Looks like Toki doesn't have any dora.

00:07:34.550 --> 00:07:36.350
Neither does anyone else.

00:07:36.890 --> 00:07:38.850
It's just like Hiroko's data suggested.

00:07:43.360 --> 00:07:46.770
<i>If the dora really gather in her hand,</i>

00:07:46.770 --> 00:07:50.110
<i>it means that her hand is 
that much more readable.</i>

00:07:50.440 --> 00:07:54.460
<i>More, based on her weird playing 
style in the first round,</i>

00:07:55.650 --> 00:07:58.020
<i>she's pretty much incapable 
of throwing a dora away.</i>

00:08:11.100 --> 00:08:11.940
Ron.

00:08:13.100 --> 00:08:14.340
That's 1300 points.

00:08:15.280 --> 00:08:18.220
The first winner of the second 
round is Senriyama Girls'.

00:08:18.610 --> 00:08:21.310
That was a rather strange play though.

00:08:21.310 --> 00:08:23.690
Oh? How so?

00:08:24.590 --> 00:08:26.190
Matsumi Kuro from Achiga 
could've reached tenpai

00:08:26.190 --> 00:08:28.230
if she'd just discarded that dora.

00:08:28.650 --> 00:08:32.160
Then Senriyama's Onjouji didn't 
go for a three-sided wait

00:08:32.160 --> 00:08:34.860
and opted for a single 
middle tile wait instead.

00:08:35.140 --> 00:08:37.960
I don't know if it's strange or what.

00:08:37.960 --> 00:08:38.870
Oh?

00:08:40.880 --> 00:08:42.090
Kuro.

00:08:43.600 --> 00:08:45.250
You can't discard a dora?

00:08:50.600 --> 00:08:53.760
You mean when someone's declared riichi?

00:08:55.150 --> 00:08:56.890
That's not what I mean.

00:08:57.450 --> 00:08:59.710
Whenever I discard a dora,

00:08:59.710 --> 00:09:03.930
I don't get a single one for 
the next few games.

00:09:05.420 --> 00:09:06.770
That's weird.

00:09:07.450 --> 00:09:10.800
When my mom was still alive,

00:09:10.800 --> 00:09:14.530
she always told me that I need 
to value my dora more.

00:09:15.340 --> 00:09:19.030
I always remember that 
every time I get one.

00:09:20.660 --> 00:09:22.340
Since I was little,

00:09:22.340 --> 00:09:24.660
I valued my dora more 
than a winning hand.

00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:27.350
At some point,

00:09:27.350 --> 00:09:30.650
I got the feeling that it caused 
more dora to come to me.

00:09:33.240 --> 00:09:36.610
Nodoka, aren't you going to 
say what you always say?

00:09:36.610 --> 00:09:37.670
What?

00:09:37.670 --> 00:09:39.920
That's so superball or whatever.

00:09:40.480 --> 00:09:42.510
I don't believe in that 
kind of coincidence,

00:09:43.090 --> 00:09:44.930
but I don't want to deny her feelings.

00:09:45.280 --> 00:09:46.770
What are you talking about?

00:09:46.770 --> 00:09:47.610
Superball!

00:09:47.610 --> 00:09:49.020
It's superstition!

00:09:52.180 --> 00:09:55.690
<i>Kuro, if you let your hand 
get tied up with dora,</i>

00:09:55.690 --> 00:09:58.350
<i>there's a higher chance 
you'll deal an unsafe tile</i>

00:09:58.350 --> 00:09:59.710
<i>toward the end of the game.</i>

00:10:00.260 --> 00:10:03.200
East Hand 1
Seventh turn

00:10:04.660 --> 00:10:06.580
<i>I can't see any dora.</i>

00:10:21.560 --> 00:10:22.420
Ron.

00:10:23.170 --> 00:10:24.640
2,600 points.

00:10:25.860 --> 00:10:28.390
<i>She was waiting on a weird tile again, 
just before I could have...</i>

00:10:28.390 --> 00:10:31.400
<i>What's the deal with her?!</i>

00:10:31.400 --> 00:10:34.320
<i>That's such a shady play style.</i>

00:10:34.840 --> 00:10:37.410
<i>Onjouji Toki from Senriyama Girls' gets</i>

00:10:37.410 --> 00:10:40.860
<i>another win off of Achiga Girls' 
Academy's Matsumi Kuro.</i>

00:10:42.210 --> 00:10:44.700
Off Kuro-chan again?

00:10:44.700 --> 00:10:47.940
Could the girl from Senriyama 
be targeting her deliberately?

00:10:47.940 --> 00:10:50.830
She's probably figured 
out how Kuro plays.

00:10:51.130 --> 00:10:54.440
She threw away a five-sided wait 
only to wait for an 8 of bamboo.

00:10:54.440 --> 00:10:56.280
It really looks like that's 
the only explanation.

00:10:56.280 --> 00:10:57.710
It's just a coincidence!

00:10:57.710 --> 00:11:00.130
That just happened out of luck!

00:11:00.980 --> 00:11:02.380
<i>Is it just a coincidence?</i>

00:11:02.950 --> 00:11:07.260
<i>It's certainly possible to estimate 
Kuro's playing style from her data.</i>

00:11:07.780 --> 00:11:11.010
<i>But is it really just that?</i>

00:11:11.890 --> 00:11:14.270
That was another 
strange wait, wasn't it?

00:11:14.710 --> 00:11:17.140
I saw her play records for the 
regional competition, too.

00:11:17.140 --> 00:11:18.900
She always plays like this.

00:11:19.460 --> 00:11:22.180
Whenever she switches her 
wait to something weird,

00:11:22.180 --> 00:11:24.210
she wins off of someone 
in the next turn.

00:11:24.210 --> 00:11:26.310
Whenever she called a tile 
for no apparent reason,

00:11:26.310 --> 00:11:28.870
it ruined someone else's tsumo win.

00:11:28.870 --> 00:11:30.160
She's basically...

00:11:30.160 --> 00:11:31.750
...predicting the future?!

00:11:33.330 --> 00:11:35.460
I wouldn't go that far.

00:11:35.460 --> 00:11:38.830
There were times where it 
backfired two turns later,

00:11:38.830 --> 00:11:43.090
but it's almost never backfired 
in the first turn.

00:11:43.560 --> 00:11:47.230
You're saying this hunch of hers 
only works for one turn?

00:11:47.230 --> 00:11:49.190
I don't really know,

00:11:49.190 --> 00:11:50.860
but what I do know is that she

00:11:50.860 --> 00:11:53.100
very rarely declares riichi even 
when she legally could.

00:11:53.720 --> 00:11:59.360
When she does declare 
riichi, well then...

00:12:06.570 --> 00:12:07.830
Riichi.

00:12:07.830 --> 00:12:09.700
<i>Onjouji's declared riichi!</i>

00:12:09.700 --> 00:12:10.910
<i>Here it is!</i>

00:12:11.310 --> 00:12:13.100
<i>She called riichi!</i>

00:12:13.100 --> 00:12:16.790
<i>If the same thing happens that 
I saw in her match history...</i>

00:12:16.790 --> 00:12:18.670
<i>Someone has to call a tile!</i>

00:12:19.000 --> 00:12:21.450
Many pros have come out of the

00:12:21.450 --> 00:12:23.940
western stronghold, Senriyama.

00:12:23.940 --> 00:12:25.640
But just in the fall of last year,

00:12:25.640 --> 00:12:28.190
they unexpectedly placed 
an unknown player

00:12:28.190 --> 00:12:29.930
in their ace position...

00:12:32.580 --> 00:12:33.640
That was...

00:12:35.760 --> 00:12:36.530
Tsumo.

00:12:37.050 --> 00:12:38.150
4,000 from all.

00:12:38.830 --> 00:12:40.070
Onjouji Toki!

00:12:40.500 --> 00:12:42.280
The girl who can see one turn ahead!

00:12:47.010 --> 00:12:48.390
No way...

00:12:48.390 --> 00:12:49.620
Kuro!

00:12:50.100 --> 00:12:51.930
One turn ahead?

00:12:53.290 --> 00:12:54.870
Is that even...

00:13:07.390 --> 00:13:08.580
Unbelievable.

00:13:09.190 --> 00:13:11.350
She really drew her winning 
tile in one turn.

00:13:11.620 --> 00:13:13.760
This truly does make it seem like

00:13:13.760 --> 00:13:15.850
she can see one turn into the future.

00:13:15.850 --> 00:13:19.030
Oh, but you know, it could 
just be a coincidence.

00:13:19.030 --> 00:13:20.640
But if she can kind of feel

00:13:20.640 --> 00:13:23.110
what'll happen in the next turn,

00:13:23.490 --> 00:13:25.610
then wouldn't that mean she usually

00:13:25.610 --> 00:13:28.320
gets to tenpai faster than anybody else?

00:13:29.740 --> 00:13:30.660
Riichi.

00:13:32.050 --> 00:13:33.410
<i>Twice in a row?!</i>

00:13:33.410 --> 00:13:35.160
<i>Come on!</i>

00:13:35.660 --> 00:13:37.570
<i>So this is how the nationals are...</i>

00:13:37.570 --> 00:13:39.920
<i>When you get close to the 
top of 10,000 players...</i>

00:13:41.130 --> 00:13:44.500
Tsumo. 2,700 from all.

00:13:44.500 --> 00:13:46.430
<i>...there are some unbelievable players!</i>

00:13:49.470 --> 00:13:51.100
Kuro-chan...

00:13:51.360 --> 00:13:52.770
Kuro-chan!

00:13:52.770 --> 00:13:54.050
Kuro-chan, keep going!

00:13:54.050 --> 00:13:55.530
Go get them, senpai!

00:13:55.530 --> 00:13:56.790
Kuro-chan!

00:13:56.520 --> 00:13:59.130
Matsumi-senpai!

00:13:56.790 --> 00:13:59.130
Come on!

00:13:59.130 --> 00:14:00.610
Kuro-chan!

00:14:08.050 --> 00:14:09.280
First Players' Match, Second half 
 Last hand
Dealer: Matsumi Kuro

00:14:14.320 --> 00:14:16.290
<i>I have to do something!</i>

00:14:27.730 --> 00:14:30.800
<i>Renchan as dealer... for that I need...</i>

00:14:27.730 --> 00:14:30.800
(renchan - if the dealer wins, she stays dealer)

00:14:34.350 --> 00:14:36.270
<i>to win with speed!</i>

00:14:37.430 --> 00:14:38.890
<i>Speed.</i>

00:14:46.600 --> 00:14:48.070
<i>Speed...</i>

00:14:49.420 --> 00:14:50.110
Pon!

00:14:51.620 --> 00:14:52.490
Pon.

00:14:53.880 --> 00:14:54.870
<i>Strike fast!</i>

00:14:58.920 --> 00:14:59.500
Pon!

00:15:00.980 --> 00:15:01.960
<i>Strike fast!</i>

00:15:06.840 --> 00:15:07.880
Riichi.

00:15:19.290 --> 00:15:20.100
Tsumo.

00:15:20.540 --> 00:15:23.020
2,000. 3,900.

00:15:24.290 --> 00:15:26.280
And the first players' match is finished!

00:15:31.530 --> 00:15:34.120
G-Good game.

00:15:34.890 --> 00:15:36.730
I'm tired!

00:15:38.590 --> 00:15:40.760
I'm exhausted.

00:15:47.360 --> 00:15:50.130
Looking at the results of this 
match, Senriyama's Onjouji Toki

00:15:50.130 --> 00:15:53.640
dominated with more than 40,000 points.

00:15:50.970 --> 00:15:52.810
Toki, are you okay?

00:15:52.810 --> 00:15:53.680
Yeah.

00:15:53.680 --> 00:15:54.780
I'm fine.

00:15:53.680 --> 00:15:57.360
Koshigaya Girls' has managed to end with 
more points than they began with,

00:15:54.780 --> 00:15:55.660
I'm glad.

00:15:57.360 --> 00:15:59.140
but it looks like Kentani High 
School and Achiga Girls' Academy

00:15:59.140 --> 00:16:01.390
are off to a rough start.

00:16:01.390 --> 00:16:05.050
That was quite a rough turn of 
events for Dragon Road-chan.

00:16:05.990 --> 00:16:09.180
<i>Looking back, it seems 
her light defenses got</i>

00:16:09.180 --> 00:16:11.400
<i>targeted by more than just Senriyama.</i>

00:16:13.160 --> 00:16:14.250
Kuro...

00:16:14.740 --> 00:16:16.490
I'm going to get her!

00:16:16.870 --> 00:16:18.260
Let's all go!

00:16:18.260 --> 00:16:19.330
Wait...

00:16:20.460 --> 00:16:23.200
I'll go.

00:16:23.730 --> 00:16:25.130
Leave it to me.

00:16:26.230 --> 00:16:27.580
Yuu-nee...

00:16:27.580 --> 00:16:28.840
Will you be okay?

00:16:30.420 --> 00:16:32.950
Yes. I'm her older sister.

00:16:37.200 --> 00:16:38.540
Kuro-chan.

00:16:39.590 --> 00:16:41.600
Onee-chan...

00:16:41.840 --> 00:16:46.360
You seem down. 
That's not like you.

00:16:49.650 --> 00:16:51.330
But...

00:16:51.330 --> 00:16:55.360
I lost so many of our precious points.

00:16:55.870 --> 00:16:57.860
Don't worry.

00:16:57.860 --> 00:17:00.310
Akado-san said that the first match

00:17:00.310 --> 00:17:04.050
is an ace position full of monster players,

00:17:04.050 --> 00:17:06.130
and that it often gets rough,

00:17:06.590 --> 00:17:10.460
so nobody is blaming you at all.

00:17:10.850 --> 00:17:14.140
Besides, I'm going to go out there

00:17:14.140 --> 00:17:16.390
and get them back for us.

00:17:20.580 --> 00:17:23.680
Onee-chan!

00:17:26.400 --> 00:17:27.900
Hot...

00:17:27.900 --> 00:17:29.460
I'm sorry.

00:17:29.460 --> 00:17:32.120
Thanks so much.

00:17:32.120 --> 00:17:35.580
Uh, uh, do you want to 
wipe them with my scarf?

00:17:35.580 --> 00:17:36.910
I'm fine.

00:17:41.360 --> 00:17:42.390
Here you go.

00:17:43.280 --> 00:17:45.210
I'm totally fine.

00:17:45.210 --> 00:17:46.870
All right, then.

00:17:48.590 --> 00:17:52.120
I guess maybe I'm a little tired.

00:17:53.920 --> 00:17:55.740
That was two East-South matches...

00:17:56.400 --> 00:17:58.010
how many more?

00:17:58.010 --> 00:17:59.810
Four more.

00:17:59.810 --> 00:18:01.760
Then we'll have won Nationals.

00:18:02.090 --> 00:18:03.720
Really, that's it?

00:18:03.720 --> 00:18:06.810
That's even easier than winning 
the North Osaka tournament.

00:18:07.400 --> 00:18:08.820
Big words.

00:18:09.270 --> 00:18:10.900
<b>Senriyama Girls'</b>

00:18:11.200 --> 00:18:12.520
We're back!

00:18:12.520 --> 00:18:13.520
Oh.

00:18:13.520 --> 00:18:14.740
Good job!

00:18:14.740 --> 00:18:16.530
How are you feeling?

00:18:17.000 --> 00:18:19.540
Luckily, I was able to win 
without much trouble.

00:18:22.660 --> 00:18:25.590
The next match will begin momentarily.

00:18:25.590 --> 00:18:28.200
We ask each school's second player

00:18:27.280 --> 00:18:30.290
Well, looks like it's my turn.

00:18:28.200 --> 00:18:30.290
to come to the tournament hall.

00:18:30.790 --> 00:18:32.290
Good luck, Izumi!

00:18:32.290 --> 00:18:34.420
I won't cause you any worry.

00:18:34.420 --> 00:18:37.100
Please enjoy your rest.

00:18:37.760 --> 00:18:40.060
The seed, Senriyama Girls',

00:18:40.060 --> 00:18:42.020
finished the first players' 
match with a giant lead,

00:18:42.020 --> 00:18:45.650
but the game isn't over yet.

00:18:45.650 --> 00:18:47.960
Coming now from Senriyama Girls'

00:18:47.060 --> 00:18:52.790
Senriyama Girls' (North Osaka)
 1st Year - Second Player
Nijou Izumi

00:18:47.960 --> 00:18:49.550
we have Nijou Izumi.

00:18:49.550 --> 00:18:51.020
She's the only 1st year regular

00:18:51.020 --> 00:18:52.770
on this veteran team.

00:18:52.840 --> 00:18:53.820
<b>Koshigaya Girls'</b>

00:18:53.660 --> 00:18:55.690
Coming in second in the last match,

00:18:55.690 --> 00:18:57.020
Here I go!

00:18:55.690 --> 00:18:58.280
Koshigaya Girls' is sending 
Asami Hanako to play.

00:18:56.590 --> 00:18:59.240
Koshigaya Girls' (Saitama)
3rd year - Second Player
Asami Hanako

00:18:59.260 --> 00:19:03.240
<b>Kentani</b>

00:18:59.920 --> 00:19:03.900
Kentani High School is in third 
place with 89,600 points,

00:19:03.900 --> 00:19:07.840
but this team can certainly 
turn things around.

00:19:07.840 --> 00:19:10.370
Their second player is Yorifuji Sumiko.

00:19:08.120 --> 00:19:10.370
Kentani High School (Hyougo)
2nd year- Second Player
Yorifuji Sumiko

00:19:10.520 --> 00:19:12.540
I'm so sorry!

00:19:12.540 --> 00:19:17.140
That was more than enough 
against Senriyama's Onjouji!

00:19:17.140 --> 00:19:18.800
Let's do our best in 
this second match, too!

00:19:18.800 --> 00:19:21.650
Good luck, senpai!

00:19:21.650 --> 00:19:22.590
Give 'em hell!

00:19:23.270 --> 00:19:25.510
Okay! Here I go.

00:19:25.940 --> 00:19:27.230
Are you all right?

00:19:27.730 --> 00:19:29.520
Can you go back by yourself?

00:19:29.990 --> 00:19:31.050
Yeah.

00:19:31.050 --> 00:19:32.070
Okay.

00:19:32.070 --> 00:19:33.440
Then I'm going.

00:19:34.520 --> 00:19:37.170
The last place team, having fallen 
behind by 40,000 points,

00:19:37.170 --> 00:19:38.790
is Achiga Girls' Academy.

00:19:38.790 --> 00:19:41.240
Achiga Girls' Matsumi Yuu is the older sister

00:19:41.240 --> 00:19:43.950
of their first player, Matsumi Kuro.

00:19:45.230 --> 00:19:47.110
She's wearing a scarf! A scarf!

00:19:47.110 --> 00:19:49.460
In the middle of summer!

00:19:49.460 --> 00:19:53.710
Is she going to be able to regain 
the points her sister lost?

00:19:54.360 --> 00:19:57.420
The second players' match 
will be starting shortly.

00:20:00.160 --> 00:20:01.760
I wish everyone a good game.

00:20:01.760 --> 00:20:04.300
Go easy on me.

00:20:06.250 --> 00:20:09.080
I look forward to playing you.

00:20:15.190 --> 00:20:16.570
<i>Kuro-chan.</i>

00:20:17.590 --> 00:20:18.660
<i>Watch...</i>

00:20:21.770 --> 00:20:23.070
Onee-chan...

00:20:26.830 --> 00:20:28.350
<i>Her first discard was the 3 of bamboo,</i>

00:20:29.480 --> 00:20:32.210
<i>just like Funakubo-senpai said!</i>

00:20:32.210 --> 00:20:33.250
What?

00:20:33.250 --> 00:20:35.050
Her draws are not balanced?

00:20:35.050 --> 00:20:36.000
Indeed!

00:20:36.450 --> 00:20:38.620
I was thinking about 
those Matsumi sisters...

00:20:38.620 --> 00:20:40.170
If the younger sister has the tendency

00:20:40.170 --> 00:20:41.970
to be such a dora bomb,

00:20:41.970 --> 00:20:45.360
I figured that the older 
sister must also have

00:20:45.360 --> 00:20:47.510
some sort of weird characteristic.

00:20:47.870 --> 00:20:49.880
But there wasn't anything particularly

00:20:49.880 --> 00:20:51.910
weird while we watched her play.

00:20:51.910 --> 00:20:55.020
No, she's a little like me.

00:20:55.470 --> 00:20:58.600
Oh, you mean she's sickly, too.

00:20:58.600 --> 00:21:00.030
That's not what I meant.

00:21:00.900 --> 00:21:03.350
Sometimes she plays like she can sense

00:21:03.350 --> 00:21:06.280
which tiles are about to come to her.

00:21:06.280 --> 00:21:08.160
That's exactly it!

00:21:08.160 --> 00:21:09.510
So was that the simple

00:21:09.510 --> 00:21:11.720
little program you made this morning?

00:21:11.720 --> 00:21:14.740
Using subject Matsumi 
Yuu's match history,

00:21:14.740 --> 00:21:18.040
I derived the distribution of tiles 
that end up in her hand.

00:21:18.430 --> 00:21:20.550
If you draw 70,000 times,

00:21:20.550 --> 00:21:25.970
you should get each of the 
34 tiles about 2,000 times.

00:21:25.970 --> 00:21:27.050
Should.

00:21:27.280 --> 00:21:29.760
But in just five East-South matches?

00:21:29.760 --> 00:21:32.170
With such a small sample,

00:21:32.170 --> 00:21:34.810
everybody's distribution will be weird.

00:21:34.810 --> 00:21:37.880
But without even looking deeper into it,

00:21:37.880 --> 00:21:40.350
Matsumi Kuro had a lot of dora.

00:21:40.350 --> 00:21:42.820
You're right. That's kind of scary.

00:21:42.820 --> 00:21:44.950
So? What about the older sister?

00:21:45.570 --> 00:21:47.820
It was a little like this.

00:21:50.570 --> 00:21:52.330
Does Izumi know about this?

00:21:52.600 --> 00:21:53.830
Of course!

00:21:53.830 --> 00:21:56.210
I told her first thing in the morning.

00:21:53.890 --> 00:21:56.210
6th turn

00:22:01.090 --> 00:22:05.310
<i>Both her and her sister's 
hands are easy to read.</i>

00:22:05.310 --> 00:22:07.470
<i>I guess I'll take this match home, too!</i>

00:22:13.350 --> 00:22:14.980
Yorifuji-san, fight!

00:22:31.760 --> 00:22:34.320
<i>The points they took from Kuro-chan...</i>

00:22:35.880 --> 00:22:39.460
<i>I'm going to get them 
back, no matter what!</i>

00:22:41.520 --> 00:22:43.580
R-Riichi.

00:24:04.960 --> 00:24:19.890
<b>Recovery</b>

00:24:06.920 --> 00:24:08.610
Ako, you're always quick to set up.

00:24:08.610 --> 00:24:11.050
If you have reds, you've got to 
focus on speed rather than yaku.

00:24:11.050 --> 00:24:12.710
You've got to polish your sense of flow.

00:24:12.710 --> 00:24:14.040
I'm polishing it, too.

00:24:14.040 --> 00:24:15.350
Really?

00:24:15.350 --> 00:24:17.790
Since I get cold easily, 
I like the hot water flow.

00:24:17.790 --> 00:24:19.280
Different flow...
